---
import {
  INSTALL_PACKAGES,
  KEY_FINGERPRINT,
  KEY_PATH,
  MIN_RYOKU,
  PACMAN_CONF,
  SETUP,
  TARBALL_COMMAND,
  TARBALL_URL,
  TRUST_KEY,
} from "../data/install";
import CodeLine from "./CodeLine.astro";
---

<section id="install" class="section" aria-labelledby="install-title">
  <header class="head" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow"><b>Install</b> four steps</p>
    <h2 id="install-title" class="display">Install Crate for Ryoku</h2>
  </header>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li data-reveal>
      <h3>Trust the signing key</h3>
      <p>
        Crate signs every package and the repository database. Download <a class="u-link" href={KEY_PATH}>the
        key</a>, check that it reads <code class="fpr">{KEY_FINGERPRINT}</code>, then add it to pacman and sign it
        locally.
      </p>
      <CodeLine code={TRUST_KEY} label="the key commands" />
    </li>
    <li data-reveal>
      <h3>Add the repository</h3>
      <p>Append it to <code>/etc/pacman.conf</code>.</p>
      <CodeLine code={PACMAN_CONF} label="the repository block" />
    </li>
    <li data-reveal>
      <h3>Install the packages</h3>
      <p>The mod and the Crate desktop app.</p>
      <CodeLine code={INSTALL_PACKAGES} label="the install command" />
    </li>
    <li data-reveal>
      <h3>Set it up</h3>
      <p>Applies the rice, the icons, the terminal and the bar plugin. <code>crate-for-ryoku uninstall</code> takes you back.</p>
      <CodeLine code={SETUP} label="the setup command" />
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="other" data-reveal>
    <div>
      <h3>AUR</h3>
      <p>Not yet. The packages go to the AUR once its registration reopens; until then this repository is the source.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Release tarball</h3>
      <p>
        Download it from <a class="u-link" href={TARBALL_URL}>the latest release</a>, unpack it and run
        <code>{TARBALL_COMMAND}</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Requirements</h3>
      <p>
        Ryoku {MIN_RYOKU} or newer on Arch. The Crate desktop app needs a Crate server. A few style
        details need Ryoku changes on their way upstream.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* A link inside running text takes the text's size. */
  .u-link {
    font-size: inherit;
  }

  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 36px;
    margin: 0 0 64px;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
    max-width: 820px;
  }

  .steps li {
    counter-increment: step;
    display: grid;
    /* a long command scrolls inside its block instead of widening the step */
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 10px;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .steps h3::before {
    content: counter(step, decimal-leading-zero);
    margin-right: 14px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--cyan-hi);
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 21px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  /* forty hex digits wrap on a phone instead of widening the step */
  .fpr {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .other {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 240px), 1fr));
    gap: 28px;
    padding-top: 36px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .other div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
    align-content: start;
  }
</style>
